---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="React Native Wrapper Docs — TesterLoop"
  description="Integrate TesterLoop into React Native and Expo Dev Client Android apps with @testerloop/react-native and one manifest tag."
  canonicalPath="/docs/sdk/react-native"
>
  <article class="card">
    <h1>TesterLoop React Native Wrapper</h1>
    <p>
      Android-only wrapper (<code>@testerloop/react-native</code>) via React Native autolinking;
      safe no-op on iOS and Web (<code>platforms.ios = null</code> so <code>pod install</code> skips it).
      No JavaScript/TypeScript code required.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Install package</h2>
    <pre><code>npm install @testerloop/react-native
# or: pnpm add @testerloop/react-native</code></pre>

    <h2>2. Add APP_KEY (<code>android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml</code>)</h2>
    <pre><code>&lt;meta-data
    android:name="io.testerloop.APP_KEY"
    android:value="tl_pk_your_app_key_here" /&gt;</code></pre>

    <p>
      Ensure <code>minSdkVersion</code> is <strong>23 or higher</strong> in <code>android/build.gradle</code>.
      For Expo managed projects, run <code>npx expo prebuild --platform android</code> first (TesterLoop requires native Android builds, not Expo Go).
    </p>

    <h2>3. Optional JS / TS API</h2>
    <pre><code>import &#123; TesterLoop &#125; from '@testerloop/react-native';

const status = await TesterLoop.status(); // 'NOT_ENROLLED' | 'TRACKING' | 'DISABLED'
await TesterLoop.setEnabled(false);</code></pre>

    <p>
      Also available: <a href="/docs/sdk/android">Android Kotlin SDK</a> ·
      <a href="/docs/sdk/flutter">Flutter Plugin</a> ·
      <a href="/llms-full.txt">/llms-full.txt</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
